The P1 Gefion HPC is a sandbox with on-demand H100 GPUs on [Gefion](https://dcai.dk/gefion). Use
it to develop, test and pilot a workload on the hardware generation it will scale up on. Full 8-GPU
production nodes need separate funding, such as a Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF) compute voucher or
another allocation. A workload that already runs here is what you apply with.

## Getting Access

### Who's eligible?

**Requirements:** PhD or higher (exceptions may apply), valid Danish university email, and
registered P1 affiliation.

### Do I need to talk to someone first?

No. The optional [workload survey](p1:surveyPage) tells the P1 compute coordinator about your
workload, and helps us plan production nodes if your project scales.

### How do I sign up?

1. Request P1 affiliation in [your P1 profile](p1:profile) (**Update Profile** in the header). P1
   staff approve it.
2. Fill in the sandbox sign-up form below. A DCAI team member then contacts you with a DCAI
   username and initial-setup-password.

<EmbedForm
  title="P1 Gefion Sandbox Sign-up Form"
  src="{GEFION_SIGNUP_FORM_URL}?embed=true"
  href={GEFION_SIGNUP_FORM_URL}
  description="Requires an approved P1 affiliation."
/>

### What if I don't qualify?

<AccessException />

## Connecting

```bash
aicentre check -p gefion --connect
```

`aicentre check` shows what your machine needs for Gefion: the Host block for `~/.ssh/config`
and when to sign in to DCAI again. Then it tests the login. DCAI's documentation has the
details.

## Using the Cluster

The sandbox runs Slurm. Submit GPU work as batch jobs instead of holding an interactive session
open.

- Every job names the Slurm account it is charged to. P1's default account is `iu_0096`
  (`--account=iu_0096`). A project with its own account uses that one instead.
- Nodes have 2 TB of memory, so size `--mem` for the data a job loads, not its GPUs.
- The P1 partition is on Gefion's open system. The login node reaches public git hosts and package
  indexes.
- Large transfers use the SFTP endpoint `xfer.dcai.dk`. To get your public IP whitelisted, send
  [DCAI support](mailto:support@dcai.dk) the output of `curl ifconfig.io`.

From the gallery:

- [VS Code on the login node](/gallery/rem-lgn/)
- [moving code and data](/gallery/xfr-dat/) on and off the cluster

See [every example that runs on P1 Gefion HPC](/gallery/?provider=gefion).

## Policy & Support

### What are the limits?

<ClusterQuotas slug="gefion" />

- 16 H100 GPUs in total, shared by all sandbox users
- User accounts are individual and non-transferable
- An account can belong to one or more Gefion projects

Limits may change to meet the needs of P1 students and faculty.

<Aside type="note" title="GDPR Compliance">

The P1 Gefion HPC is GDPR-compliant, so projects with personal data can run here. Have the
data-processing paperwork in place, and agree the details with DCAI and the compute coordinator,
before you upload any.

</Aside>

### How much storage do I get?

Home directories hold 25 GB, so keep datasets and checkpoints in your project space (500 GB
default). Data sent to the SFTP endpoint lands in a staging area first and counts twice until you
delete the staged copy.

Use cluster storage as working space, not an archive. Keep code in git and a second copy of
anything you cannot regenerate on institutional storage or your own machine. Before a project
ends, ask the compute coordinator what to move off.

### What if I need more GPUs?

The default limit is 2 concurrent jobs of at most 2 GPUs each. When GPUs are idle on P1's two
NVIDIA DGX H100 nodes (account `iu_0096`), you can go past it. Check what is free with `sinfo` and
submit the larger job. No request is needed.

<Aside type="caution">

Jobs beyond the default limits can be cancelled when demand picks up. You are responsible for
checkpointing, so a cancelled job resumes instead of starting over.

</Aside>

<GpuAllowance selfServeDocumented />

